xxHash: load NEON vectors with memcpy instead of a misaligned dereference (AArch64 GCC)

On AArch64 with GCC, XXH_vld1q_u64() read 16 bytes as `*(uint64x2_t const *)ptr`.
uint64x2_t needs 16-byte alignment, but the input and the secret stripes (secret + 8*n)
are not 16-byte aligned, so this is undefined behaviour. UBSan (GCC 14, -fsanitize=undefined,
any -O level) stops at xxhash.h:4150 "load of misaligned address ... requires 16 byte
alignment" for every XXH3 input longer than 240 bytes. Clang and the other XXH_VECTOR paths
are not affected (they use vld1q_u8 / _mm_loadu_si128).

A memcpy into a uint64x2_t is defined for any alignment. GCC 14 -O2 compiles it to the same
single `ldr q` as the dereference (identical instruction counts), so speed and hash values
do not change.

Engine-local patch (DENG-358), applied by tools/vendor/vendor.py. Report upstream:
https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash (no issue exists as of 2026-10; xxHash dev still has the
dereference). Drop this patch when a pinned release has the fix.

diff --git a/xxhash.h b/xxhash.h
--- a/xxhash.h
+++ b/xxhash.h
@@ -4139,15 +4139,21 @@ typedef uint64x2_t xxh_aliasing_uint64x2_t XXH_ALIASING;
  * *conditionally* safe (`vld1` has an alignment bit like `movdq[ua]` in x86).
  *
  * GCC for AArch64 sees `vld1q_u8` as an intrinsic instead of a load, so it
- * prohibits load-store optimizations. Therefore, a direct dereference is used.
+ * prohibits load-store optimizations. Therefore, a plain load is used: a
+ * memcpy into a uint64x2_t, which GCC compiles to the same single `ldr q`.
+ * A direct dereference of a `uint64x2_t const*` would also compile to that,
+ * but the input and the secret are not 16-byte aligned, so it is undefined
+ * behaviour (UBSan: "load of misaligned address").
  *
  * Otherwise, `vld1q_u8` is used with `vreinterpretq_u8_u64` to do a safe
  * unaligned load.
  */
 #if defined(__aarch64__) && defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)
-XXH_FORCE_INLINE uint64x2_t XXH_vld1q_u64(void const* ptr) /* silence -Wcast-align */
+XXH_FORCE_INLINE uint64x2_t XXH_vld1q_u64(void const* ptr)
 {
-    return *(xxh_aliasing_uint64x2_t const *)ptr;
+    uint64x2_t v;
+    XXH_memcpy(&v, ptr, sizeof(v));
+    return v;
 }
 #else
 XXH_FORCE_INLINE uint64x2_t XXH_vld1q_u64(void const* ptr)
